            "review_title": "Review at Summer Experiment",
            "review_text": "Jerome L\nSan Juan, Philippines48 contributions\n1\nNot like your usual cocktail bars - in a bad way.\nJan 2026 • Couples\nOverhyped bar - arguably the worst “top” bar in HCMC. They don’t even serve WATER. So basic.\n\nThis was my last bar in Vietnam and they didn’t do Vietnam any justice. Such a bad representation of the country., and I’ve been to more than 10 bars in the past 4 days. They all served water, great drinks, and great hospitality,\nAll the top bars i went to -\nHanoi:\nHafflington, Hudson Rooms, Track 61, Nê, Use Bar, Workshop 14,\n\nHCMC: \nThe Pi, Engima Mansion, Hybrid, Stir\n- all of them were MUCH BETTER and at the very least - served water, which is a basic expectation of any GOOD bar.\n\nAnd all of them I got to really connect with the bartenders and even add them as friends on instagram — here was the only only one I felt like I could not because the staff were very robotic and don’t have any personal touch. They didn’t even ask for our names even when I asked for theirs (which I normally do when I go bars!)\n\nI spent more than 1 million by myself and they didn’t even have the decency to provide water???\n\nI eventually paid for the glass of water and even paid more for it and they didn’t give any change or official receipt - I think that’s against consumer protection laws but I didn’t have time to argue anymore.\n\nThis is such an absurd and overhyped bar. Do not come here: worst in HCMC. Hospitality was super bad and mid.\n\nHonestly, I don’t want to come back to HCMC just because of this.\nRead more\nWritten January 7, 2026",
