            "review_text": "DiscoverWorkTravel\nCologne, Germany162 contributions\n0\nfantastic\nApr 2024 • Couples\nReview Highlights:\n\nInventive Cocktails: Summer Experiment is tucked away (up a slightly tired staircase) in what seems to be a residential building. But trust me, it’s worth the search! The lounge space exudes a cool vibe, and their cocktails are extremely inventive. They play with a wide variety of spirits, fruits, flowers, and spices. Try the “Mule Met The Apricot” for a tangy, ginger-infused delight.\nHidden Gem: Like many bars and coffee shops in the city, Summer Experiment is discreetly hidden without clear signs. However, it gained recognition on the World’s Best 50 list, and now you know why! It’s just a 2-minute walk from… well, wherever you are.\nHappy Hour: The happy hour prices are amazing, making it affordable for both tourists and locals. Friendly bartender Ethan and the service staff ensure you have a great time. Plus, they serve some of the rare gins alongside their creative cocktails.\nOverall Verdict: If you’re up for an adventure in mixology, head to Summer Experiment. The combination of great drinks, good vibes, and reasonable prices makes it a must-visit spot in Ho Chi Minh City! 🍹🌟\nRead more\nValue\nService\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 21, 2024",
